# PROJECT SYNOPSIS

## Title: Smart City Issue Reporting Platform

### 1. Introduction

Smart cities aim to provide efficient public services and improve the quality of life of citizens. However, issues such as potholes, overflowing garbage bins, water leakages, damaged streetlights, drainage problems, and broken roads are often reported through phone calls or traditional complaint systems, leading to delays and a lack of transparency.

This project proposes a web-based Smart City Issue Reporting Platform that allows citizens to report civic problems online by uploading photographs, providing descriptions, selecting issue categories, and specifying their locations. The platform enables government authorities and administrators to manage complaints, assign them to appropriate departments, monitor their progress, and ensure timely resolution.

The primary goal of this project is to create a centralized digital platform that improves communication between citizens and municipal authorities while making civic complaint management more organized, accessible, and transparent.

### 2. Problem Statement

Existing civic complaint management systems often suffer from slow response times, inefficient complaint handling, limited tracking facilities, and a lack of communication between citizens and government authorities.

Citizens may face difficulties reporting public infrastructure problems and tracking the progress of their complaints. Similarly, authorities may find it challenging to organize complaints, identify responsible departments, assign tasks, and monitor unresolved issues.

Therefore, there is a need for a centralized online platform that simplifies complaint registration, improves complaint management, and provides transparency throughout the resolution process.

### 3. Proposed Solution

The proposed system is a full-stack web application that provides a centralized platform for citizens to report civic issues and for government authorities to manage and resolve them efficiently.

Citizens can register and log in to the platform, upload photographs of civic problems, select the appropriate issue category, enter a detailed description using a text field, and provide their location. Each submitted complaint will be stored in the database and assigned a unique complaint ID for tracking purposes.

Administrators can access a dedicated dashboard to view all submitted complaints, filter them based on category, location, and status, assign complaints to the appropriate departments or field officers, and update their progress.

Citizens can track their complaints through different status updates, such as Pending, In Progress, and Resolved.

The system will provide a simple, user-friendly, and transparent approach to managing civic issues without requiring artificial intelligence integration.

### 4. Objectives

- Develop a full-stack web application for reporting civic issues.
- Provide secure user registration and login functionality.
- Allow citizens to upload photographs of public infrastructure problems.
- Provide a text area for describing civic issues in detail.
- Enable citizens to select issue categories and report locations.
- Generate unique complaint IDs for tracking purposes.
- Develop an administrative dashboard for complaint management.
- Allow administrators to assign complaints to appropriate departments.
- Provide real-time or regularly updated complaint status tracking.
- Maintain complaint history and records in a centralized database.
- Improve communication, transparency, and accountability between citizens and authorities.

### 5. Key Features

#### A. Citizen Portal

- Secure user registration and login.
- User profile management.
- Submit civic complaints through an online form.
- Upload images of reported problems.
- Enter detailed problem descriptions using a text area.
- Manually select complaint categories.
- Select or provide the location of the issue.
- Receive a unique complaint ID.
- Track complaint status.
- View previous complaints and their history.
- Receive notifications regarding complaint updates.

#### B. Complaint Management System

- Store all submitted complaints in the database.
- Maintain unique identification numbers for complaints.
- Organize complaints according to their categories.
- Maintain complaint status (Pending, In Progress, Resolved, Rejected).
- Allow administrators to prioritize complaints manually.
- Assign complaints to appropriate departments or officers.
- Maintain records of complaint updates and resolutions.

#### C. Government/Admin Dashboard

- Secure administrator login.
- View all registered complaints.
- Filter complaints by category, location, and status.
- View uploaded complaint photographs and descriptions.
- Assign complaints to departments or field officers.
- Update complaint status.
- Manage registered users.
- Monitor pending and resolved complaints.
- View complaint statistics and generate reports.
- Visualize reported issues using maps and charts.

